      dealing: "Deal 5 cards to each player. The 'Trump Caller' (usually right of dealer) looks at their 5 cards and calls the Trump Suit (Rung). Then the remaining cards are dealt (8 more to each) for a total of 13 each.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Trump Call**: The Caller names the suit (Rung) based on their first 5 cards. 2. **The Lead**: Caller leads the first trick. 3. **The Trick**: Players must follow suit. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins. 4. **Accumulation Rule**: When a player wins a trick, they DO NOT collect the cards yet. The cards remain face down in the center heap. 5. **Double Sar Rule**: If the SAME player wins the *next* trick (two in a row), they capture the ENTIRE heap (all previous uncollected tricks) and place them in their team's pile. 6. **13th Trick**: The winner of the 13th (final) trick captures strictly that trick plus any uncollected heap remaining.",
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Be-Ranga is a traditional partnership trick-taking game scored with match points rather than monetary antes.',
      deal: 'The initial distribution of thirteen cards per player is performed by the system dealer at the start of each hand.',
      reveal_market: 'All 52 cards are distributed among the players; there is no public market or shared pool of cards in this game.',
      buy_market: 'Players must succeed using only the hand they were dealt; there is no option to buy or swap cards from a market.',
      buy_stock: 'The entire deck is distributed at the start of the hand; no cards remain in stock to be purchased during play.',
      fold: 'Partnerships must participate in all thirteen tricks to satisfy the requirements of the accumulation mechanic.',
      check: 'The game uses a trick-taking structure with accumulation rather than a vying structure where checks would apply.',
      call: 'There is no bet to match in this game; competition is based on winning consecutive tricks to capture the heap.',
      bet: 'Progress is tracked via trick count and game points rather than through the wagering of chips or currency.',
      raise: 'The stakes of the round are fixed; there are no wagering rounds where players could increase the value.',
      declare: 'Hand resolution is based purely on trick capture without a separate declaration phase for melds.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands stay private until cards are played into tricks; there is no full reveal phase during the hand.',
